WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:01.110
- I would safely say, yeah,

00:00:01.110 --> 00:00:02.892
my bull(beeping) detector
is pretty good by now.

00:00:02.892 --> 00:00:04.031
(laughing)

00:00:04.031 --> 00:00:06.614
(upbeat music)

00:00:07.430 --> 00:00:09.110
Telltale signs of an underage person,

00:00:09.110 --> 00:00:12.030
typically you get the
person who is very edgy

00:00:12.030 --> 00:00:13.630
when they show up and
they really don't know

00:00:13.630 --> 00:00:14.670
exactly how things work,

00:00:14.670 --> 00:00:16.950
and they're kind of just
anxious for no reason,

00:00:16.950 --> 00:00:18.980
and then, of course, they
hesitantly hand your their ID,

00:00:18.980 --> 00:00:20.420
and they kind of just sit there and smile.

00:00:20.420 --> 00:00:21.430
- Oh, their body language.

00:00:21.430 --> 00:00:23.623
Most people are pretty good at lying,

00:00:23.730 --> 00:00:24.860
but their body isn't.

00:00:24.860 --> 00:00:25.810
- When they're walking up,

00:00:25.810 --> 00:00:28.943
they're, uh, here, and no eye contact.

00:00:28.960 --> 00:00:31.960
Usually, I find that people
will stand up straight

00:00:31.960 --> 00:00:33.520
and they're like, yes, that's me,

00:00:33.520 --> 00:00:34.720
and they'll look at the card,

00:00:34.720 --> 00:00:35.880
whereas the other one will be like,

00:00:35.880 --> 00:00:37.940
hey, yo, and kind of look away,

00:00:37.940 --> 00:00:40.353
so I mean, those are
just some of the signs.

00:00:40.578 --> 00:00:42.310
(upbeat music)

00:00:42.310 --> 00:00:44.510
- There's certain things
on one ID that's real

00:00:44.510 --> 00:00:46.160
that you won't find on a fake ID,

00:00:46.440 --> 00:00:47.330
and vice versa.

00:00:47.330 --> 00:00:48.520
- Some of the things we look for,

00:00:48.520 --> 00:00:49.760
when we're looking for a fake ID

00:00:49.760 --> 00:00:52.690
would definitely be
laminated pieces of plastic

00:00:52.690 --> 00:00:55.440
or pieces of paper that
have absolutely zero traits

00:00:55.510 --> 00:00:56.343
of an actual ID.

00:00:56.580 --> 00:00:58.890
- Most IDs do have a special actual tag

00:00:58.890 --> 00:01:01.030
that you can see in certain lighting.

00:01:01.030 --> 00:01:03.110
- Here in California
is if you have a light,

00:01:03.110 --> 00:01:05.950
you have the California
bear outlined in the back,

00:01:05.950 --> 00:01:07.140
and if you hold it up,

00:01:07.140 --> 00:01:08.400
you can see that outline,

00:01:08.400 --> 00:01:10.543
whereas the fakes tend to not have it.

00:01:10.694 --> 00:01:12.960
(upbeat music)

00:01:12.960 --> 00:01:16.240
Well, actually, at my first
job, in 2011, a couple,

00:01:16.240 --> 00:01:19.250
either blatantly not
recognizing their surroundings,

00:01:19.250 --> 00:01:20.780
or deliberately not caring,

00:01:20.780 --> 00:01:24.230
and starting to get it on
while other people are around,

00:01:24.230 --> 00:01:25.227
so I had to politely tell them,

00:01:25.227 --> 00:01:27.117
"Hey, look, this is not the spot for that.

00:01:27.117 --> 00:01:28.783
"I feel you, have a good time.

00:01:28.817 --> 00:01:30.640
"Just move it on, take it elsewhere."

00:01:30.640 --> 00:01:32.520
- I've seen a lot of people hook up.

00:01:32.520 --> 00:01:33.820
Pretty much wherever they can it in,

00:01:33.820 --> 00:01:36.223
seen that on, I would
say, an everyday basis.

00:01:36.580 --> 00:01:38.800
It's not really crazy anymore.

00:01:38.800 --> 00:01:40.105
It's just the norm to me now.

00:01:40.105 --> 00:01:40.938
(upbeat music)

00:01:40.938 --> 00:01:43.763
- Starting a fight,
and probably stripping,

00:01:43.840 --> 00:01:44.833
just getting naked.

00:01:44.960 --> 00:01:46.350
- Undermining the fact that we're here,

00:01:46.350 --> 00:01:48.020
and we're doing a job, and
we're here to do a job,

00:01:48.020 --> 00:01:50.160
and making sure that you're
allowing us to do so.

00:01:50.160 --> 00:01:52.100
- Get out of line, and try
to be aggressive with you

00:01:52.100 --> 00:01:53.103
for no reason.

00:01:53.250 --> 00:01:54.083
It does happen.

00:01:54.083 --> 00:01:55.395
You get macho people,

00:01:55.395 --> 00:01:57.410
whether it's women or men,

00:01:57.410 --> 00:01:59.040
who just have a bad attitude,

00:01:59.040 --> 00:02:00.400
and wanna take it out on you.

00:02:00.400 --> 00:02:03.283
- Someone not having their
forms of ID like they should,

00:02:03.520 --> 00:02:05.510
and just trying to talk me up.

00:02:05.510 --> 00:02:06.640
Oh, you're so handsome!

00:02:06.640 --> 00:02:07.520
You're so cute!

00:02:07.520 --> 00:02:09.610
It's like, um, appreciate the compliment,

00:02:09.610 --> 00:02:12.210
but you know, I still
need that form of ID,

00:02:12.210 --> 00:02:13.140
if you don't mind.

00:02:13.140 --> 00:02:15.140
- Honestly, pet names and things like that

00:02:15.140 --> 00:02:17.340
are probably the easiest
way to piss me off.

00:02:17.880 --> 00:02:20.093
Oh, things like big boy, big John.

00:02:21.570 --> 00:02:22.403
Accurate.

00:02:22.481 --> 00:02:23.770
(laughing)

00:02:23.770 --> 00:02:25.410
- First impressions,
coming up to the door,

00:02:25.410 --> 00:02:27.200
it'll always make a huge statement.

00:02:27.200 --> 00:02:28.033
- Being polite.

00:02:28.033 --> 00:02:29.870
You actually don't have
to say much to a bouncer.

00:02:29.870 --> 00:02:31.620
Just make sure you have your ID card.

00:02:31.620 --> 00:02:33.260
- Probably just being
prepared and not having

00:02:33.260 --> 00:02:34.720
a bunch of assholes that you're with.

00:02:34.720 --> 00:02:36.090
- Don't be getting out of line.

00:02:36.090 --> 00:02:37.510
Just have a good time,

00:02:37.510 --> 00:02:39.900
and don't be destructive or disruptive

00:02:39.900 --> 00:02:40.844
and causing a scene.

00:02:40.844 --> 00:02:42.670
(upbeat music)

00:02:42.670 --> 00:02:44.160
- The best excuse I've ever gotten

00:02:44.160 --> 00:02:46.020
for forgetting an ID was definitely

00:02:46.020 --> 00:02:47.220
they said their dog ate it,

00:02:47.220 --> 00:02:49.453
which we all know is a crock of shit.

00:02:49.480 --> 00:02:51.400
- Literally the worst excuse you could say

00:02:51.400 --> 00:02:53.033
is I forgot my ID.

00:02:53.170 --> 00:02:55.020
There's no excuses for forgetting it.

00:02:55.200 --> 00:02:56.033
Just bring it.

00:02:56.033 --> 00:02:58.448
(jazz music)

00:02:58.560 --> 00:03:00.660
Most likely not, but
depending on the situation,

00:03:00.660 --> 00:03:02.413
every situation is different,

00:03:02.550 --> 00:03:05.070
and sometimes, it can be reevaluated

00:03:05.270 --> 00:03:07.250
and possibly be let back in,

00:03:07.250 --> 00:03:10.263
but in most instances,
if you're escorted out,

00:03:10.510 --> 00:03:11.729
you're not coming back in.

00:03:11.729 --> 00:03:13.880
(upbeat music)

00:03:13.880 --> 00:03:16.260
I would say the bull(beeping)
detector that I have

00:03:16.260 --> 00:03:18.530
is pretty on par, and you'd be lucky

00:03:18.530 --> 00:03:19.530
